  "payload": {
    "rawResponseText": "For a **luxury hotel with a for-sale branded-residences component in the Caribbean or Latin America**, developers typically consider the following brands.\n\n### Core luxury shortlist\n\nThese usually receive the strongest initial consideration because of their residential track records, buyer recognition and ability to support premium pricing:\n\n- **Four Seasons**\n- **The Ritz-Carlton**\n- **St. Regis**\n- **Rosewood**\n- **Waldorf Astoria**\n- **Mandarin Oriental**\n- **One&Only**\n- **Park Hyatt**\n\nThe Ritz-Carlton and Four Seasons are particularly established in branded residences globally. Both also have substantial resort-residential experience in Mexico, Central America and the Caribbean. ([pdf.savills.com](https://pdf.savills.com/documents/Branded-Residences-Annual-Report-24-25.pdf?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Ultra-luxury and low-density resort brands\n\nOften evaluated for secluded villa, estate-home or environmentally sensitive resort concepts:\n\n- **Aman**\n- **Ritz-Carlton Reserve**\n- **One&Only**\n- **Six Senses**\n- **Rosewood**\n- **Auberge Resorts Collection**\n- **Montage**\n- **Banyan Tree**\n\nThese brands generally fit projects with larger residences, low density, significant privacy, high service levels and compelling natural settings. Regional precedents include One&Only Mandarina, Six Senses Belize and Grenada, Rosewood Mayakoba and Auberge-operated residential resorts in Los Cabos. ([oneandonlyresorts.com](https://www.oneandonlyresorts.com/private-homes?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Luxury lifestyle brands\n\nRelevant where the development is more design-, entertainment-, culinary- or nightlife-oriented:\n\n- **W Hotels**\n- **EDITION**\n- **Nobu**\n- **Andaz**\n- **Thompson**\n- **SLS**\n- **Mondrian**\n- **SO/**\n- **Kimpton**\n- **Pendry**\n\nNobu has been especially active regionally, with residences in Los Cabos and projects in Tulum, Punta Cana and Barbuda. Accor’s SLS and Mondrian brands are also regularly considered for lifestyle-oriented mixed-use projects. ([nobuhotels.com](https://www.nobuhotels.com/the-nobu-residence-collection/?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Broader luxury and upper-upscale alternatives\n\nThese can be attractive where the residential pricing is strong but not at the very top of the market, or where distribution and loyalty-system strength are especially important:\n\n- **JW Marriott**\n- **The Luxury Collection**\n- **Conrad**\n- **LXR Hotels & Resorts**\n- **Fairmont**\n- **Raffles**\n- **InterContinental**\n- **Regent**\n- **Kimpton**\n- **Curio Collection by Hilton**\n- **Viceroy**\n\nHilton currently uses Waldorf Astoria, Conrad, LXR, Curio and several other brands for residential projects; its regional portfolio includes projects in Costa Rica, Los Cabos, Panama, Turks and Caicos, Anguilla, Belize, Colombia and Mexico. ([stories.hilton.com](https://stories.hilton.com/branded-residential-by-hilton-fact-sheet?utm_source=openai))\n\n### Regionally relevant or market-specific brands\n\nDepending on the country and target buyer profile, the following may also be considered:\n\n- **Fasano** — particularly strong relevance in Brazil\n- **Banyan Tree** — established recognition in Mexican resort markets\n- **Viceroy** — lifestyle-luxury resort positioning\n- **1 Hotels** — sustainability-led lifestyle positioning\n- **Belmond** — exceptionally strong leisure identity, although less established as a conventional residence-licensing platform\n- **Leading Hotels of the World affiliation** — useful for an independent concept, but not equivalent to a fully managed residential brand\n\n## Practical first-call list\n\nFor a conventional high-end Caribbean or Latin American resort, I would normally begin with:\n\n1. Four Seasons  \n2. Ritz-Carlton or Ritz-Carlton Reserve  \n3. St. Regis  \n4. Rosewood  \n5. Waldorf Astoria  \n6. Mandarin Oriental  \n7. One&Only  \n8. Park Hyatt  \n9. Six Senses  \n10. Auberge or Montage  \n11. W, EDITION or Nobu for a lifestyle concept  \n12. Fairmont, Conrad/LXR or Luxury Collection for a broader luxury positioning  \n\nThe final shortlist should be driven by **site accessibility, residence pricing, hotel key count, villa-versus-condominium mix, buyer source markets, required rental program and expected service-charge burden**. Territorial availability is also critical: a brand may like the project but be restricted by an existing hotel or development agreement nearby. Latin America and the Caribbean remain important growth markets for branded residences, so competition for appropriate sites—and among brands for attractive projects—is increasing. ([knightfrank.com](https://www.knightfrank.com/research/article/2025-09-08-the-global-branded-residence-survey-2025?utm_source=openai))",
